        },
        "text_WTKQpB": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "text": "<p>To overhaul the checkout experience using Shopify's Checkout Branding API, I executed a checkoutBrandingUpsert GraphQL mutation to implement a custom design system without relying on legacy CSS overrides. The architecture leverages isolated color schemes mapped to specific checkout zones—such as the header, main input area, and order summary—to visually compartmentalize the page. I utilized the API's typography controls to integrate custom fonts and force heading capitalizations, while manipulating global corner radius parameters to generate fully rounded, pill-shaped buttons. Finally, I explicitly nested button color overrides within each individual scheme payload to guarantee that any custom Checkout UI extension blocks seamlessly inherit the native storefront styling.</p>"
          }
        },
